WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:07.150
The Game of Thrones Season 7 trailer begins,
as all great trailers do, with a geography

00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:12.349
lesson. Queen Cersei stands on a map, and
says there are enemies to her east, to her

00:00:12.349 --> 00:00:17.870
west, to her south, and to her north – there’s
Daenerys Targaryen with her invading army,

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:22.780
there’s King Euron Greyjoy with his ironborn
fleet, there’re the Sand Snakes and Olenna

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:28.230
in the Reach and in Dorne, and in the north,
there’s King Jon Snow. We learn a lot about

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:32.230
each of these sides in the trailer, and bout
other cool stuff besides, so let’s have

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:36.699
a quick look at what this all means for the
future of Game of Thrones.

00:00:36.699 --> 00:00:41.980
First off, Daenerys Targaryen finally arrives
at Westeros. This is a moment that Dany has

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:47.110
dreamed of for years , that fans have awaited
for years, ever since the first book came

00:00:47.110 --> 00:00:53.760
out back in ’96. Daenerys was born here
at Dragonstone, ancestral home of the Targaryen

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:58.649
dynasty that had ruled Westeros for three
centuries – until Robert Baratheon took

00:00:58.649 --> 00:01:04.339
over, and Dany had to flee with her brother
Viserys. All her life Dany longed to return

00:01:04.339 --> 00:01:10.250
to her home, and to her birthright the Iron
Throne, and now, after six seasons and five

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:16.261
books and twenty long years, her time has
finally arrived to conquer Westeros. This

00:01:16.261 --> 00:01:22.300
table in Dragonstone was made by Dany’s
ancestor Aegon three hundred years ago – a

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:27.311
map with “no borders” to show that the
Seven Kingdoms is truly “One realm, for

00:01:27.311 --> 00:01:33.520
one king to rule alone” – or, in this
case, one queen – there ain’t room for

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:39.000
two on the Iron Throne. So to defeat Queen
Cersei, Dany brings with her three dragons,

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:45.670
a Dothraki horde, an Unsullied army – fire
and blood. Dany says she was “born to rule

00:01:45.670 --> 00:01:51.140
the Seven Kingdoms”, but is she even the
good guy here? From another perspective, she’s

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:56.350
a crazy dragon lady from across the sea, attacking
the Kingdoms with foreign soldiers, burning

00:01:56.350 --> 00:02:02.450
people alive with flying monsters – is she
really the hero? Dany’s often compared to

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:08.610
her father, the cruel Mad King Aerys. Will
Dany be a force for peace, or will she go

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:14.850
down her dad’s dark path? Fortunately, Dany
has many supporters and advisors around her,

00:02:14.850 --> 00:02:20.100
including Grey Worm of the Unsullied, and
Missandei, who get it on in the trailer – despite

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:25.210
the fact that Grey Worm is a eunuch. And there’s
Tyrion Lannister, who has valuable political

00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:30.610
experience in King’s Landing, and who has
a curious relationship with Dany’s dragons

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:36.440
– some fans think that Tyrion might ride
a dragon. Dany also has Varys, though he’s

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:41.400
barely visible in the trailer – and other
characters like Daario and Kinvara aren’t

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:44.420
there at all, they’ve been left in Meereen
– these last seasons of Thrones move so

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:48.940
fast there isn’t even time to kill off the
minor characters before they’re cut from

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:56.030
the story. But someone else we do see is Melisandre,
she’s at Dragonstone, which is a surprise.

00:02:56.030 --> 00:03:01.000
Last we saw Mel, she was exiled from Winterfell
by Jon and Davos for that whole child murder

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:07.270
kerfuffle last season – seems that Mel then
went to Dragonstone where Dany is. Mel has

00:03:07.270 --> 00:03:12.120
a pretty flaky record when it comes to supporting
leaders – first she says Stannis is the

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:17.690
saviour, then Jon – maybe now she’ll support
Daenerys, who other red priests say is the

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:24.370
hero Azor Ahai. Dany and Mel both love flame,
so they should get along like a house on fire

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:31.310
– or a girl on f– mm. Anyway, Dany has
a great squad and a huge army, and in the

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:36.700
trailer, she goes on the attack.
We see Cersei’s Lannister soldiers attacked

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:42.970
by Daenerys’ Unsullied, in a castle that
looks unfamiliar. It’s got Lannister heraldry

00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:49.330
painted on an archway though so this might
be Casterly Rock, the home base of the Lannisters

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:55.069
which we’ve never seen before in the books
or show. The Rock is a massive fortress built

00:03:55.069 --> 00:04:00.720
into a mountain in the westerlands, and it’s
apparently never been taken before. If Casterly

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:06.540
Rock falls to Daenerys, that would be a huge
blow to House Lannister. This spot on the

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:12.850
map, by the way, seems to read C A – maybe
supporting the idea that this place is Casterly

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:17.130
Rock.
So Daenerys is Cersei’s eastern enemy. Her

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:23.130
enemies to the south are Dany’s allies – the
Sand Snakes of Dorne and Olenna of the Reach.

00:04:23.130 --> 00:04:27.440
These guys don’t actually appear in the
trailer, which is a strong hint they might

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:33.190
not last long in Season 7. The first big Sand
Snakes episode was the least popular episode

00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:37.290
in Game of Thrones history, and ever since
the showrunners seem to be pretending that

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:42.960
the Dorne storyline never happened – with
only a brief couple scenes in Season 6. So

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:47.820
the Sand Snakes’ll probably be quickly swept
under the rug in Season 7 – though hopefully

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:53.180
Olenna Tyrell still has some fight in her.
Olenna’s whole family was murdered by Cersei

00:04:53.180 --> 00:04:59.060
last season – so now Olenna has nothing
to lose – she’s out for revenge. Also,

00:04:59.060 --> 00:05:04.360
we see Ellaria Sand making out with Yara Greyjoy,
which is fun – though, the last person who

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:10.080
Ellaria kissed, Cersei’s daughter Myrcella,
caught a pretty bad case of death by poison,

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:15.800
so Yara might wanna be careful where she sticks
her bits – but also, Cersei has not forgotten

00:05:15.800 --> 00:05:22.400
the murder of Myrcella by the Sand Snakes.
There are a lot of scores to settle in Season

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:25.340
7.
Another battle in the trailer seems to take

00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:30.479
place in the south – because Dany’s Dothraki
are fighting men not from House Lannister,

00:05:30.479 --> 00:05:36.030
but from House Tarly – this bowman looks
just like the Tarly heraldry. House Tarly

00:05:36.030 --> 00:05:41.720
is led by Randyll Tarly, said to be one of
the greatest military minds in Westeros . However,

00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:47.080
it looks like Randyll makes the mistake of
trying to fight the Dothraki not in a castle

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:52.840
but in the open field. That is, like, the
one thing you should never do against mounted

00:05:52.840 --> 00:05:58.200
Dothraki – cause these guys can run your
ass down, shooting arrows from horseback , jumping

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:04.620
from one horse to another, duel-wielding arakhs,
running literal circles around you – this–

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:09.810
just– you don’t want that. So Randyll
fucked up, and will probably die, which actually

00:06:09.810 --> 00:06:16.020
is pretty lucky for Randyll’s son Samwell.
Sam, if you remember, took Randyll’s favourite

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:21.320
toy last season, the Valyrian steel sword
Heartsbane. And Randyll might not forgive

00:06:21.320 --> 00:06:26.010
that – he’s threatened to kill Sam before,
and after the theft of his beloved sword,

00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:31.820
he might finally decide to quote “hunt [Sam]
down like the pig” he is . So maybe not

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:37.639
such a bad thing if Sam’s dad dies. Meanwhile,
Sam can keep studying in the Citadel of the

00:06:37.639 --> 00:06:44.009
maesters. He and Gilly might uncover secrets
in the Citadel library – in this promo image,

00:06:44.009 --> 00:06:50.030
Gilly is reading a text about Azor Ahai, the
hero prophesied to save the world. The Citadel

00:06:50.030 --> 00:06:55.830
is home to Westeros’ greatest experts on
history, and astronomy, and on medicine – which

00:06:55.830 --> 00:07:01.660
could be very important for Jorah Mormont
– in the trailer we see his arm emerge from

00:07:01.660 --> 00:07:07.919
within a wooden door, badly infected with
the disease greyscale. Jorah is slowly turning

00:07:07.919 --> 00:07:13.840
into a stony zombie, but there might be hope
of a cure at the Citadel. And this raises

00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:18.350
some really cool possibilities. Cause in the
books, there’s a character called Victarion

00:07:18.350 --> 00:07:24.530
Greyjoy who gets an infected wound in his
arm. He’s healed in a magical ritual, and

00:07:24.530 --> 00:07:31.150
afterwards, his arm is left bloody and blackened,
charred and smoking – but apparently “stronger”

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:36.790
than ever . Maybe the curing of Jorah’s
infected arm will do something similar – give

00:07:36.790 --> 00:07:42.539
him a red smoking superpowered arm just like
Victarion, and like Hellboy, and the Ninja

00:07:42.539 --> 00:07:49.240
Gaiden guy, and C-3PO. This might not be likely,
but it would be super cool.

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:53.490
So that’s what’s going on in the south.
Cersei’s enemies in the west seem to refer

00:07:53.490 --> 00:08:00.180
to the ironborn under King Euron Greyjoy – that’s
a Greyjoy ship we see in the trailer. Cersei

00:08:00.180 --> 00:08:06.130
calls Euron an enemy, but an alliance between
the two is possible – that might be Euron

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:11.250
in Cersei’s throne room in the trailer.
Cersei desperately needs so allies – surrounded

00:08:11.250 --> 00:08:16.970
as she is on by enemies on all sides. And
with the Iron Islands behind him, Euron could

00:08:16.970 --> 00:08:22.380
prove a powerful friend. In the trailer we
see him attack what seems to be Daenerys’

00:08:22.380 --> 00:08:27.740
fleet – the Targaryen, Tyrell and Martell
ships we saw at the end of Season 6. And this

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:33.479
battle could be huge – Theon Greyjoy is
there, Yara and Ellaria are probably there,

00:08:33.479 --> 00:08:38.479
and judging by all the fire, Dany’s dragons
might be involved. We’ve seen the dragons

00:08:38.479 --> 00:08:44.620
kick ass at sea before, but ironborn are famously
dangerous on water, and Euron no doubt has

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:49.950
some tricks up his sleeve. So this naval battle
could get pretty crazy.

00:08:49.950 --> 00:08:55.580
So Euron may be a useful ally for Cersei,
but otherwise she’s running pretty low on

00:08:55.580 --> 00:09:01.370
friends – having blown up half the capital
last season. As tensions rise and her enemies

00:09:01.370 --> 00:09:06.490
close in, it’ll be interesting to see if
Cersei shows any remorse or regret over her

00:09:06.490 --> 00:09:11.640
crimes – or if she’ll remain defiant to
the end. Speaking of which, there’s a lot

00:09:11.640 --> 00:09:17.089
of speculation over how Cersei may die. A
prophecy in the books suggests that Cersei’ll

00:09:17.089 --> 00:09:22.520
be killed by her brother. Cersei thinks this
means Tyrion – but some fans think Jaime

00:09:22.520 --> 00:09:27.440
will be the one to kill his sister. So maybe
Cersei’s most faithful protector will prove

00:09:27.440 --> 00:09:33.500
to be Gregor Clegane, the undead Mountain,
who now looks like a medieval Darth Vader

00:09:33.500 --> 00:09:38.800
in some new black armour. It’s cool how
the armour has an image of Cersei’s crown

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:44.550
on the chest – previous Kingsguard armour
has shown a Targaryen dragon, a King’s crown,

00:09:44.550 --> 00:09:49.930
or the Faith’s star – this emblem puts
Cersei front and centre. Cersei’s been a

00:09:49.930 --> 00:09:56.310
focus of a lot of the HBO promos lately – this
season might a big one for her.

00:09:56.310 --> 00:10:00.080
So we’ve seen Cersei’s enemies to the
east south and west – when she speaks of

00:10:00.080 --> 00:10:05.550
her enemies to the north, we get a shot of
Arya Stark travelling alone. The show has

00:10:05.550 --> 00:10:10.430
spent two seasons training Arya as an assassin,
but with Walder Frey dead, her priority now

00:10:10.430 --> 00:10:16.670
seems to be to return home to Winterfell . Ever
since Season 1, Arya has been cruelly separated

00:10:16.670 --> 00:10:22.250
from her family, and it’ll be a hugely emotional
moment for her to see Sansa, and Bran and

00:10:22.250 --> 00:10:27.750
Jon again. First, though, she might reunite
with another close friend – the direwolf

00:10:27.750 --> 00:10:33.100
Nymeria, who Arya had to leave in the riverlands
back in Season 1. There are hints in the books

00:10:33.100 --> 00:10:38.620
that while Arya has been off training, Nymeria’s
been busy too – growing from a cute lil

00:10:38.620 --> 00:10:45.480
doggo into a “monstrous” man-eating she-wolf,
leading a huge pack of wolves across the riverlands.

00:10:45.480 --> 00:10:50.880
Nymeria is not just a symbol of Arya’s Stark
heritage – she’s a symbol of how Arya’s

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:57.610
changed from an innocent young girl to violent,
ruthless killer. Hopefully she’ll find some

00:10:57.610 --> 00:11:03.160
peace this season. Also speaking of Bran,
he and Meera aren’t in the trailer but they’re

00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:07.810
presumably still heading down to Winterfell.
Since Benjen dropped them off a fair distance

00:11:07.810 --> 00:11:13.760
short of the Wall, Meera has a long way to
drag Bran home. Which could get tricky with

00:11:13.760 --> 00:11:18.310
the zombies chasing them, though on the upside
when they arrive Meera’s glutes’ll be

00:11:18.310 --> 00:11:23.019
incredible. But at Winterfell itself, we see
Cersei’s main northern enemies – King

00:11:23.019 --> 00:11:29.770
Jon Snow, and Sansa Stark, with Brienne, and
the lords of the north, and Davos, and Littlefinger,

00:11:29.770 --> 00:11:34.950
lurking down in the shadows. We see him in
the Winterfell crypts with Jon and Jon slams

00:11:34.950 --> 00:11:40.060
Petyr up against a wall. Did Littlefinger
just say something about Jon’s mother? They

00:11:40.060 --> 00:11:45.110
are standing next to the statue of Lyanna
Stark – and while we found out last season

00:11:45.110 --> 00:11:51.220
that Jon is Lyanna’s son, Jon doesn’t
know that yet – but maybe Littlefinger does?

00:11:51.220 --> 00:11:57.710
Also, Jon attacking Petyr mirrors a scene
in Season 1 when Ned did the same thing. Starks

00:11:57.710 --> 00:12:03.329
are touchy. Littlefinger is also whispering
in the ear of Sansa, who he seems to trying

00:12:03.329 --> 00:12:08.940
to turn against Jon. On the one hand, Petyr
has a point – Sansa is the oldest trueborn

00:12:08.940 --> 00:12:14.520
child of Ned Stark – apart from Bran who
everyone thinks is dead – so by rights it’s

00:12:14.520 --> 00:12:19.810
Sansa, not Jon, who should rule the north.
On the other hand, Petyr is a sociopathic

00:12:19.810 --> 00:12:25.740
scheming creep who sold Sansa to the Boltons,
killed Sansa’s aunt Lysa, betrayed Sansa’s

00:12:25.740 --> 00:12:30.620
father Ned, and partly caused the War of the
Five Kings in the first place, so it’s about

00:12:30.620 --> 00:12:36.220
goddamn time that someone killed this guy
already. Davos, meanwhile, plays the voice

00:12:36.220 --> 00:12:41.080
of reason, reminding everyone that all this
petty politics is pointless in the face of

00:12:41.080 --> 00:12:45.709
the coming war with the white walkers. It’s
kinda funny how the Starks have so suddenly

00:12:45.709 --> 00:12:50.300
come to trust this random southerner Davos,
but it’s a good thing they do, cause he’s

00:12:50.300 --> 00:12:55.420
one of the only people talking sense in this
series. The HBO promos this year make it clear

00:12:55.420 --> 00:13:00.180
that the walkers and the wights are the big
threat to Westeros. And in the trailer, it

00:13:00.180 --> 00:13:05.110
looks like Jon leads a push against the walkers
– a group of people run out beyond the Wall,

00:13:05.110 --> 00:13:11.420
including Jon, and Tormund, and possibly Gendry
– see how one of the blokes has a warhammer?

00:13:11.420 --> 00:13:17.860
Gendry is the bastard son of Robert Baratheon,
who famously used a warhammer in his Rebellion.

00:13:17.860 --> 00:13:22.470
Fans have been saying for years how cool it
would be if Gendry took up a hammer and emulated

00:13:22.470 --> 00:13:26.630
his father in battle. With all the rowing
he’s been doing, he’d probably be more

00:13:26.630 --> 00:13:31.060
than strong enough – a shame the weather’s
so cold though – he’ll probably haveta

00:13:31.060 --> 00:13:36.110
keep his shirt on. Also, we know the Hound
has joined Beric and Thoros heading north

00:13:36.110 --> 00:13:40.790
– maybe those guys are in this group too.
Brienne might be there, and Benjen’s out

00:13:40.790 --> 00:13:45.709
here somewhere too – so this might just
be the greatest all-star team we’ve ever

00:13:45.709 --> 00:13:50.750
seen in Thrones, some of the best warriors
in all Westeros fighting together – they’ll

00:13:50.750 --> 00:13:57.400
need to be at their best to face the walkers,
and the wights, and the Long Night to come.

00:13:57.400 --> 00:14:02.269
So there is a huge amount of stuff happening
in Game of Thrones Season 7 – and there’s

00:14:02.269 --> 00:14:09.339
only seven episodes to fit it all in. Time
is running out to wage wars, settle scores,

00:14:09.339 --> 00:14:14.870
expose secrets, achieve ambitions, unite with
family, bring about justice, to fight to survive

00:14:14.870 --> 00:14:20.360
and to fulfil destiny. We’re well beyond
the books now, so no one knows how this’ll

00:14:20.360 --> 00:14:28.360
end – and every moment might just be a character’s
final scene. Make sure to subscribe to Alt

00:14:28.360 --> 00:14:32.720
Shift X for more on the Game of Thrones show
and books – we got videos about Arya and

00:14:32.720 --> 00:14:36.990
white walkers and Varys and Azor Ahai if you
wanna go check those out. And if you haven’t

00:14:36.990 --> 00:14:41.350
read the books before, consider buying them
with the Amazon link below. You will not regret

00:14:41.350 --> 00:14:46.930
reading deeper into Thrones. This chart is
by Swolf_of_WallStreet, this Victarion art

00:14:46.930 --> 00:14:52.930
is by Mike Hallstein, this Vader art is by
Roberto Robert – all of the links are below.

